            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Building a Slave Army</strong><br>\nOnce free, Spartacus proved to be a natural leader and quickly gathered a sizable force of rebels. His army grew as he attracted not only slaves but also those who were discontented with Roman rule. His forces were composed of various nationalities and backgrounds, united by the desire for freedom.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The War Against Rome</strong><br>\nThe slave army led by Spartacus won several battles against Roman forces. Their strategy included guerrilla tactics and swift movements, exploiting the Roman army's vulnerabilities. Spartacus's leadership and the motivation of his forces presented a formidable challenge to the Roman Republic, which had underestimated the threat posed by the revolt.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Tactics of Spartacus</strong><br>\nSpartacus showed great tactical skills in defeating Roman legions sent after him. He trained his army in the art of Roman warfare, using their own techniques against them. His success lay in his ability to adapt, use the terrain to his advantage, and turn scavenged weapons into effective tools for battle.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
